  "narrative": {
    "northStar": "The Departures Hall",
    "overview": "PackVote borrows the two faces of an airport. Dark mode is the departures board: a blue-black ground, near-black split-flap cells, cool-white type and one signal yellow. Light mode is the wayfinding sign: cool concrete grey, solid yellow panels, black type. Both themes follow `prefers-color-scheme`, and there is no toggle. Both read as public, legible information rather than decoration. The group's vote is shown as a board resolving, with flaps turning and a row going to BOARDING, not as a chart.\n\nDensity is calm. A single centred column (64rem) holds generous section gaps. Type is large and tight-tracked for statements, and monospaced for data: codes, counts, statuses. Depth comes from tone and hairline rules, not shadows. Motion is mechanical and short: tiles flip down into place, and chips slide to their new row with a long ease-out.\n\nThe product rule \"no photography or imagery anywhere\" holds visually too: there are no rasters, illustrations or hero images. The board, type and yellow carry the identity.",
    "keyCharacteristics": [
      "Two themes, one world: departures board (dark) and wayfinding sign (light).",
      "Signal yellow is the only accent, used sparingly and on purpose.",
      "Geist for statements, Geist Mono for anything a board would print.",
      "Flat, rule-separated surfaces. Shadows only on lifted interaction states.",
      "Status colors are solid fills, read the way an airport reads them: green = boarding/winner, red = eliminated."
    ],
    "rules": [
      {
        "name": "The Fill-Only Yellow Rule",
        "body": "In light mode yellow is only ever a fill. Text, focus rings, caret, active-tab underlines and accent arrows use `--color-accent-ink`, which is sign black in light and signal yellow in dark. `--color-accent-subtle` is the solid yellow in light and a dark olive (`board-yellow-subtle`) in dark. Never put yellow text or a yellow stroke on a light surface.",
        "section": "colors"
      },
      {
        "name": "The One Yellow Primary Rule",
        "body": "Exactly one yellow primary action per screen. Secondary navigation that duplicates it (for example the header \"Sign in\") is a text link, not a button.",
        "section": "colors"
      },
      {
        "name": "The Solid Status Rule",
        "body": "Status labels on the board are solid fills with their own text color (green BOARDING, red ELIMINATED, muted RUNNER-UP), so they stay legible on the yellow winner row in both themes. Green or red text on yellow fails in dark and is not allowed.",
        "section": "colors"
      },
      {
        "name": "The Contrast Floor Rule",
        "body": "Text holds at least 4.5:1 on background, surface and muted, and rings and non-text UI hold at least 3:1, in both themes. A new color pairing has to meet this before it ships.",
        "section": "colors"
      },
      {
        "name": "The Board Prints Mono Rule",
        "body": "Anything a board would print (destination codes, initials, vote counts, statuses, trip codes and PINs) is Geist Mono with tabular numerals. Prose, headings and buttons are never mono.",
        "section": "typography"
      },
      {
        "name": "The Flat-At-Rest Rule",
        "body": "Nothing casts a shadow at rest. Depth appears only when the user picks something up or opens something over the page.",
        "section": "elevation"
      }
    ],
    "dos": [
      "**Do** route every color through the `--color-*` tokens so both themes come from one class list.",
      "**Do** use `accent-ink` for any yellow-meaning text, ring, underline or icon, and `accent` only as a fill.",
      "**Do** keep exactly one yellow primary per screen.",
      "**Do** set codes, counts, initials and statuses in Geist Mono with tabular numerals.",
      "**Do** make status labels solid fills with their own text color.",
      "**Do** keep every interactive target at least 44px tall.",
      "**Do** keep motion mechanical and short (180–700ms, ease-out `cubic-bezier(0.16, 1, 0.3, 1)`), and make reduced motion show the final state."
    ],
    "donts": [
      "**Don't** put yellow text or a yellow stroke on a light surface.",
      "**Don't** put green or red text on the yellow fill.",
      "**Don't** add photography, illustrations or raster images.",
      "**Don't** add resting shadows to cards or panels.",
      "**Don't** use View Transitions for in-page movement; use FLIP with `element.animate`.",
      "**Don't** introduce a second accent hue or let warning orange drift toward the yellow."
    ]
  }
}
